  "question": "Can the Zhejiang Library official 2024 article 《郑振铎与铁琴铜剑楼藏书捐献》 be lawfully materialized as direct PDF bytes through the public article site's own current download contract, and if not, what exact access boundary is demonstrated without invoking purchase/payment flows?",
  "answer": "The first-party article/index surface and current front-end download contract are directly observed, including status=1 preflight responses and tokenized PDF, PDF_CN and PDF_Mobile route families. However, exact browser-form-equivalent POST requests to all three source-emitted route families return the same 3,241-byte HTML server 404 wrapper rather than PDF bytes. This closes the tested public route at a current access/materialization boundary only. It does not prove that no PDF exists, does not review the article full text, and adds no target-specific evidence for FID070, its Qu donation batch/date, or the 3368→3288 mechanism.",
